From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:05:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(memory): FTS5 rebuild under the write lock, owner
 pre-filter, lazy repair

- rebuild_index takes its canonical snapshot and swaps under the write lock (R4;
  8-process stress: 1-5 of 120 entries lost before, none after)
- an index failure after a successful canonical write marks the index dirty and
  is repaired before the next search instead of failing the write (R5)
- JSON values are indexed, never key names (R6); schema v2 rebuilds v1 indexes
- rebuild reports unreadable canonical files (R7)
- owner column filtered inside the FTS query, before ranking and LIMIT; the
  facade refuses a backend that cannot pre-filter (R8)
- SQLite connections are closed (R9)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EtmKEt6P3q6nMhKY8Ysc5a
